            <div xml:id="d96-a2">

                <pb facs="0259" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg163"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation from Belgian
                    newspaper.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The inspection of fresh, packed, prepared, or salted meats imported into Belgium
                    is to be the object (as officially announced) of a decree making regulations, to
                    appear soon, to be applicable from January 1.</p>
                <p>Henceforth a careful inspection of the boxes will be made on the frontiers, in
                    the ports, and in certain offices of the custom-house officers in the interior
                    of the country, such as Brussels, Liege, etc., to be designated by the
                    Government.</p>
                <p>This regulation is aiming especially at hams, boxed meats, etc., arriving in
                    large quantities from America, principally at the port of Antwerp.</p>
                <p>A tax of 15 centimes per 100 kilos of meats examined will be collected for
                    expenses of the inspection.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
